# Branch, commit and PR naming

Full convention: `CONTRIBUTING.md` → Branching / Commit messages / Pull requests.

## Branch

`<type>/DAV-<NNN>-<short-slug>`

- type ∈ `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `test`, `ci`, `chore`, `refactor`, `spike`
- `DAV-NNN` is the Linear ticket, uppercase, exactly one ticket per branch
- slug: 3–6 kebab-case words taken from the ticket title
- lowercase and hyphens except the ticket ID; no underscores or spaces
- The type follows the ticket's nature (an ADR ticket is always `docs/`)
- Never use Linear's suggested `alexandre-castro/dav-…` name
- If no ticket ID is known, ask for it before creating a branch

Examples: `feat/DAV-5-fastapi-chart-service`, `docs/DAV-1-adr-0001-c-engine-agpl`, `ci/DAV-6-docker-render-ci`, `spike/DAV-3-golden-chart-fixtures`, `chore/DAV-19-retire-streamlit`

## Commit

`<type>(DAV-<NNN>): <imperative summary, lowercase, no full stop>`

- Same type list; a review fix on a feat branch may be `fix(DAV-NNN): …`
- Say what changed in plain words
- Breaking chart-API change: `<type>(DAV-NNN)!: …` with an explanation in the body

## Pull request

- Title in the same form as the main commit
- Body: what and why, how it was tested, links to the pitch/ADR, and a final line `Closes DAV-NNN`
